ion:  \n\nIn this case, we apply the addition principle and add $7{\\color{red}y}$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7y & =1 \\\\ x-7y+7y & =1+7y \\\\ x+0 & =1+7y \\\\ x & =1+7y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd that's it! We have successfully isolated the variable ${\\color{blue}{x}}.$\n\nLet's now look at an example where we must apply the multiplication principle." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065414 #edb/ref 1065 8072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065414 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c431a781-752f-59ae-bf37-616b43771b6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065414 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
